IaC repo for a self-hosted AI agent runtime (Zet + Headroom) on OVHcloud VPS running NixOS + k3s.

***REMOVED******REMOVED*** Architecture snapshot

```
Local: opencode → Headroom(:8787) → minimax.io
VPS:   Caddy(host) → NodePort → k3s { Zet Agent, Headroom proxy, Uptime Kuma, n8n, Zitadel }
```

Caddy runs as a NixOS service on the host (not k8s Ingress). It proxies to k8s services **via NodePort**. Don't use ClusterIP or k8s Ingress — Caddy does TLS termination. NodePort mappings: Zet=30080, Uptime Kuma=30001, n8n=30002, Zitadel=30003. Headroom is ClusterIP-only (internal).

k3s is installed with `--disable traefik --disable servicelb`. Traefik conflicts with Caddy.

***REMOVED******REMOVED*** Deploy order (exact)

```
tofu apply  →  nixos-infect  →  ansible  →  nixos-rebuild  →  helmfile  →  kubectl apply
```

Use `./scripts/deploy.sh` with phase skip flags (`--skip-tofu`, `--skip-infect`, etc.). Do not skip phases or reorder.

**Pre-deploy:** create an S3-compatible object storage bucket for state first:
```bash
aws s3 mb s3://${PROJECT_NAME}-tofu-state --endpoint-url https://s3.${DATACENTER}.io.REDACTED-OVH-DOMAIN
```

**After tofu:** VPS boots Debian 12. Convert to NixOS:
```bash
ssh root@$VPS_IP 'curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elitak/nixos-infect/master/nixos-infect \
  | NIX_CHANNEL=nixos-unstable bash'
```

**NixOS:** NixOS config lives in the separate `nix-config` repo (`~/Workspace/github.com/rbelem/nix-config`). Deploy with `nixos-rebuild switch --flake path:$NIX_CONFIG_DIR#zet --target-host root@$VPS_IP`.

**Ansible secrets** are split into two playbooks: `secrets-render.yml` runs on the **workstation** (localhost, connection: local) and renders Bitwarden Secrets Manager keys to `.rendered/` (gitignored). `secrets-apply.yml` runs on the **VPS** and copies the pinned allowlist from `.rendered/` to the VPS. The SM access token never touches the VPS — bitw on the workstation reads SM via `bitw sm get` using a machine-account token (SM_ACCESS_TOKEN env or ~/.config/bitw/config). The VPS has no bitw binary, no SM token, no master password. Compromise of the VPS yields only rendered runtime secrets (bounded blast radius), not the SM access token (force multiplier).

If the workstation is unavailable, the VPS cannot self-heal secrets. Recovery: new workstation → configure SM access token → re-render.

**k8s manifests:** rsync to `/opt/k8s/` on VPS, then `kubectl apply -f /opt/k8s/manifests/zet/` etc. Namespaces are managed by Ansible (`namespace_list` in `ansible/inventory/hosts.yml`).

